    "installation": "Fixed celestial orientation, entrance direction +Z; globe sits to the right and slightly above the entrance axis, with responsive sizing that keeps its full limb inside phone viewports. Six genuine natural-color observations from the same day; a 60-second exhibition loop, not a live stream or physical orbit simulation. DSCOVR observes from about one million miles away, not from the ISS.",
    "background": "Preserve the original photographic black background. Stars are omitted in the bright-Earth view as an exposure/presentation choice, not a claim that stars cannot be seen by human observers near Earth.",
    "failureBehavior": "Keep the current frame if the next download fails; retry later. Pause the sequence clock across tab visibility changes; never blank the Earth during a transition."
  },
